Z||000000||turbo86se||09-23-2001||10:58 AM||||Last night while working my internship with the County PD, we arrested this kid for DUS. Turns out he had no idea his tags had been expired for two years. <BR>I'm filling out the paperwork on the way to the PD, when we get there, I get out with all the paperwork in my hands and walk in to the jail with my FTO and the arrestee. One of the guards stopped me and asked to see my badge, my FTO said "he's my partner and I think he forgot it."  The guard said we have to differentiate the prisioners and the officers so if you don't have a badge or wearing handcuffs, you can't be in here! LOL<P>I was never so happy to leave jail!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||09-23-2001||11:09 AM||||...thought that was a strange title for a thread.<P>Are all of the jailers like that, or was this guy just being a posterior orifice?<P>When I was working with the county, a few years back (fixed the communications stuff), it seemed that the jailers and the police seemed to look at each other with a bit of disdain.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
